/**

\page intro Introduction

\section intro_what What it is

An Fl_Dockable_Area holds a center widget, such as a 3D view, and docks
Fl_Dockable_Panel groups along its four borders: columns at the left and
right, rows at the top and bottom.  The user drags a panel by its title bar to
dock it elsewhere, to join another panel as a tab, to stack it with another,
or to float it, inside the application's window or in a window of its own.
Stripes along the borders hold buttons that show and hide panels, and a panel
may auto-hide, sliding out from its button over the center.  The application
says where each panel goes by default, hears what the user does through the
area's callback, and saves and restores the layout.

Dragging a panel out of its window and back is the work of FLTK's
Fl_Dockable_Group, so it works wherever FLTK's does, Wayland included.  This
library decides where a panel goes.

\section intro_requirements Requirements

  - FLTK 1.5 or later, with Fl_Dockable_Group and Fl_Dockable_Group::captive(),
    which are not yet part of an FLTK release; the dock-undock branch of
    https://github.com/ramcdona/fltk has them.
  - CMake 3.15 or later.
  - A C++11 compiler.

\section intro_building Building and installing

\code
cmake -S . -B build -D CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=<FLTK install> -D CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=<install>
cmake --build build
ctest --test-dir build
cmake --install build
\endcode

The library builds as fltk_dockable_area, static unless BUILD_SHARED_LIBS is
set.  These CMake options change what is built:

  - FL_DOCKABLE_AREA_BUILD_TEST (ON): the unit tests and the demo program,
    test/dockable_area.cxx.  The tests open windows, so they need a display.
  - FL_DOCKABLE_AREA_BUILD_HTML_DOCS (OFF): this manual, made with Doxygen by
    the target html.
  - FL_DOCKABLE_AREA_INSTALL_HTML_DOCS (OFF): install the manual too.

\section intro_using Using it from another project

The installed package, and the build tree, are found by CMake:

\code
find_package(Fl_Dockable_Area CONFIG REQUIRED)
target_link_libraries(myapp PRIVATE fltk::dockable_area)
\endcode

An application includes FL/Fl_Dockable_Area.H, FL/Fl_Dockable_Panel.H and,
for panels floating inside its window, FL/Fl_Dockable_Layer.H.

\section intro_version Version

FL/Fl_Dockable_Version.H gives the version as FL_DOCKABLE_AREA_MAJOR_VERSION,
FL_DOCKABLE_AREA_MINOR_VERSION and FL_DOCKABLE_AREA_PATCH_VERSION, and as one
number, FL_DOCKABLE_AREA_API_VERSION.  Fl_Dockable_Area::api_version() returns
the version of the library linked, to compare with the headers'.  A change of
the minor version keeps code built for an earlier one working; the CMake
package accepts a request for the same major and minor version.

*/
